  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 151 PM MST Mon Nov 9 2026\n\nThursday...As a ridge aloft moves further eastward across Wyoming \nand 700 mb temperatures rise to near 6 Celsius, a warming trend will \nbegin with high temperatures from the upper 50s to upper 60s.\n\nFriday...Ridging aloft moves overhead centered from western North \nDakota to eastern Colorado, with maximum temperatures similar to \nthose of Thursday.\n\nSaturday...A progressive negatively tilted shortwave trough aloft \nmoves into western Wyoming, spreading increasing mid and high level \ncloudiness across our counties, with low POPS across southern Carbon \nCounty, for rain and snow showers, including the Snowy and Sierra \nMadre Ranges. Slightly cooler with the increase in cloud cover.\n\nSunday-Monday...West to southwest flow aloft prevails, and with \nminimal low and mid level moisture, chances for precipitation will \nbe limited. Maximum temperatures will be similar each day, from the \nmid 50s to mid 60s.",
